WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.810
We asked Dr. Wakaouji to be Full Moon's producer, but...

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.860
...for some reason, he wouldn't accept the position.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.490
I tried all sorts of things, but to no avail.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.440
We were ready to give up on Dr. Wakaouji...

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.440
Or, so we thought...

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.870
But then, he suddenly said that he would be the producer!!

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.870
Looks like something Takuto said made him come to that decision.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.160
But I wonder what is was that he said?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.560
It's Shii-chan's <i>Music Power</i> !

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.520
Hi!

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.310
Covering for Shii today... Oda Shizuo!

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.800
Is everyone feeling great?

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.560
Now then, let's go straight to this week's top news!

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.860
It seems that the former Prince of Route L... {}

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.490
...is making a comeback to the music scene as Full Moon's producer. {}

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.860
Well done, Ooshige-chan.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.470
I never thought that you'd net that Wakaouji-kun.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.090
Well, let's both do out best.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:35.870
Yes!

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.420
And what's more, the song is one that everyone knows!

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.210
Route L's mystical and famous song...

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:42.090
It's a cover of <i>Eternal Snow</i>.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.420
In fact, regarding this song...

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:48.320
...Takasu Kouhei is also planning on releasing this song with the new artist Wakamatsu Madoka.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.270
How intriguing, it looks like the arrival of a powerful rival for Takasu Kouhei.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.770
For pop singers back in the sixties...

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.810
...there were often problems where different singers would sing the same song,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.130
but nowadays, we almost never see that happen.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.490
That's why this is such a hot topic.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.800
He's late.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:13.910
Ah, he's here!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.430
Wakaouji-sensei!

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:18.960
Eh?

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.250
Wakaouji-sensei...

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.370
Those clothes...

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.590
T-They don't suit me, huh?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.090
Well...

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:32.150
In order to rediscover my feelings,
I decided to try this out.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.220
No, they totally fit you!

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.430
You look cool!

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.770
R-Really?

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:37.310
Yep!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.360
Yeah, this is Takasu.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.260
How's it going?

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.820
Ah, okay, okay.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.370
I'm counting on you.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:55.620
Bye.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.290
Um, it'll be okay, right?

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.710
By okay, you mean...

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.170
...whether or not you'll win?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.130
Yes...

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.550
You want to win.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.970
That's why you called me, right?

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.180
Y-Yes.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.100
Then, get that look off your face.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.010
Have faith in me!

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.180
Y-Yes.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.390
Yes, yes, that's the look.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.560
That's the face of Wakamatsu Madoka.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.440
Yes.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.070
Yes.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.820
What?

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.940
You're already done?

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.360
That was fast.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.030
No, no, that's great.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.370
Send it my way then.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.490
What?

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.870
You've already sent it?

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.540
You're fast, Kumi-chan!

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.040
Delivered as promised.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:43.290
Y-You haven't decided?!

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.230
Yes.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.670
T-That's not a good thing, is it...

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.720
Even under these circumstances...

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:55.300
I don't think that planning ahead is what's important here.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.560
Coming up with something that everyone agrees with...

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.470
...that's what our job is.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:01.480
Even if you say that, our schedule is...

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.940
Ah, but...

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.520
If we went through a superficial routine to arrange a song...

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.190
...and only worried about the schedule, I'm not sure how things would work out.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.440
Superficial?!

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:10.150
I just...

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:11.030
Ah...

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.070
We can do something about the schedule.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:15.320
But if we don't decide on a concept...

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.030
Right?

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.330
That's right.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.620
Without that, we can't decide whom to ask to arrange it.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.910
We won't be able to decide which staff members to use either...

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.040
That's why, by all means...

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.250
...we'd like you to decide as soon as possible.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.340
<i>Full Moon</i>.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.590
Y-Yes!

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.070
<i>Full Moon</i>, through this song...

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.590
...what's the number one thing that you want to say to your fans?

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:35.220
Eh?

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.680
To my fans?

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.260
Um...

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.480
That's...

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:47.940
You don't need to be specific.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.650
Ah, okay.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.440
Um...

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:52.780
That's...

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.070
It's okay.

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.530
You don't have to answer right now.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.240
Spend some time thinking about it.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.910
I'll give you plenty of time.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.870
O-Okay...

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.750
That's it for today.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.750
See ya.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.590
Man... what are we supposed to do?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.590
I'm worried now...

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.090
Sure, he may have talent...

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:17.970
...but can he really do something like this?

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:23.100
Don't worry about it.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.390
Have faith in that doctor.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.270
Eh?

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.560
A... w-well...

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:29.150
You looked like you were fretting over something...

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:30.770
Ah, I was just thinking.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:36.450
I've been only thinking about what I wanted to say to Eichi-kun this whole time.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:39.240
I never realized it until it was mentioned, but...

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.450
What I want to say with this song...

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.540
Just what is it...?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.160
A-Ah...

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.540
That's what it was.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.420
Hmm... what you want to say, huh?

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:54.880
Let's see...

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.610
Eternal... Eternal... {}

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:57.840
Eternal... Eternal... {}

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.470
Edamame?

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.470
Of course that's not it!

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:06.060
What that doctor was saying wasn't about understanding the lyrics.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:07.560
It's something much simpler.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.230
Eh?

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:09.730
Here's an example.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.610
Let's say someone hears you sing <i>Eternal Snow</i>...

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.860
Will they burst into tears?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.530
Or will it give them courage?

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.240
Or will it force them to smile?

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:25.450
Or will it make them unable to hold in their laughter?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.500
Hey.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.710
You're overdoing it.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:30.670
Sorry.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.750
Like that.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.880
That's what he meant.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:34.710
So?

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.670
How about it?

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:36.300
Eh?

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:43.140
Well, try thinking it out carefully.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.220
Huh?

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.100
Have you found an answer?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.390
Nope...

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:28.390
Don't tell me...

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:30.440
You didn't stay up again, did you?

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.810
I slept enough.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.810
But I woke up because something was bothering me.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.650
What is bothering you?

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:42.160
What were my father's feelings when he wrote this song?

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.160
Hmm?

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:43.990
Hey...

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.790
That's right, what kind of a person was your father?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:48.160
I dunno...

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.120
Not just my father...

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.670
Nothing about my mother, either...

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.380
Even though they're your parents?

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.920
The story that the teacher at the orphanage told me was that...

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.800
...my mother died right after giving birth to me...

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.100
When I was one, my father...

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.390
...became a star in the sky...

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.390
After that...

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.650
...she also told me that my father was a musician.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:17.070
So, I started listening to the songs he wrote.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.320
And then, two years ago...

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:32.750
When Grandma took me in...

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:35.080
...I tried asking her about it, but...

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:39.670
Grandma...

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:43.510
It seems like she hates talking about my mother and father.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:47.180
Up to this every day, I haven't learned anything.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.510
In that case, let's try asking that doctor.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:50.270
Eh?

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:51.680
'Cause...

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.480
...he was in the same band as your father, right?

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.150
That's good!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.690
Let's try that, Mitsuki.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:59.860
You might discover some hints.

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.070
Well...

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.950
...I only knew the two of them while they were in the band.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.250
Your mother, Hazuki-san...

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.370
...always helped out where she could.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.170
In age...

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:20.380
...she was younger, but...

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:22.170
...she was like an older sister.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.630
A very kind person.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:30.890
Then, one day...

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:33.730
...I learned that Hazuki-san was pregnant...

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.950
She was pregnant with me, right?

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.030
Yes.

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:49.950
But...

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:53.620
...your grandmother was against their marriage.

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.750
Our leader, your father...

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.580
...Aoi-san disappeared...

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.170
...and Route L was forced to break up.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:02.590
After that...

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.340
...I had no idea what happened to Aoi-san and Hazuki-san.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.050
But then, two years ago...

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:20.190
I thought that you looked like Hazuki-san, but...

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.360
...I never suspected that it was true.

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:27.360
Of course, when I was around your grandmother, I never said a word.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.320
Father... Mother... {}

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:32.490
So?

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.910
Did you find any hints?

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:36.790
Ah... yes. Um...

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:44.050
Could it be that...

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.840
...my father wrote that song for my mother?

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:48.510
Could be.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.590
I want to know more!

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:52.800
More about my father and mother...

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:56.020
Maybe there's a memento or something that they left behind?

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.310
Let's go look!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.140
Yeah!

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:59.120
If we look around the house...

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.310
...there might be something.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:01.650
You think there is?

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.230
We're talking about your grandma here.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.230
She might have thrown it all out.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:08.280
We won't know that until we look.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:08.990
Where?

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:09.860
Ah.

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:11.350
If there is something, then is should be <i>there</i> ...

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:15.910
...in the shed!

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:35.260
Madoka can't answer the phone right now.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:38.220
Please leave a message after the tone.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:40.770
Hi!

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:41.690
Madoka?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.650
It's me.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.610
You've been so distant lately.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.650
Let's play together like we used to!

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.110
Acting this seriously...

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:52.910
It's not like you.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.050
<i>Full Moon...</i>

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:15.930
I won't lose to someone like you!

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:30.860
I might have come a little too early.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.280
Good morni...

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:39.040
Takasu-san!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.750
Takasu-san!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.870
Takasu...

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:44.520
Huh?

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:45.730
This is...

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:46.730
Wow!

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.600
It's an old issue of Ribon!

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:51.690
My mother read Ribon too, huh...

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.480
I feel so close...

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:54.320
Lemme see. Lemme see.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.450
Look at this, Meroko.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.450
This is hilarious!

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.320
Hey!

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.780
Do you think we're playing around here?!

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:01.410
Ah.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.870
That's right.

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:04.750
Come on...

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:13.800
Huh?

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:19.590
No!

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:20.350
A mouse!

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.220
It's a mouse!

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:22.890
It's a mouse!

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:23.770
Takuto!

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.770
Over here!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.390
This mouse is...!

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.270
No!

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:30.400
Takuto!

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:33.650
Look out!

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:34.320
Eh?

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.080
This is..

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:49.120
The box is the only thing here that looks particularly new.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.270
Open it up and take a look inside.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:51.210
Okay.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.500
Hey, you... that was dangerous!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:54.550
But...!

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:57.760
I was so scared!

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:58.670
Just from that...?

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.560
Ah... me?

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.440
What is it?

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:11.650
No...

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.240
This isn't me...

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.690
This is... my mother...

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.570
She looks just like you.

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.500
A jeweled music box, huh?

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:31.250
Eh?

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.250
Is it broken?

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:46.430
H-Hey...

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:47.850
This is...

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:55.570
To Hazuki, with love...

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.400
Eh?

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.230
So this is from my father?

00:16:58.230 --> 00:16:59.320
Most likely.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:04.870
The music box my father gave my mother...

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:26.430
They're inside of here...

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.810
My father's...

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.930
...feelings for my mother...

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:32.480
That's right.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.230
I want to hear them...

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.570
My father's feelings...

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:10.470
It's a good song.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:11.560
Yep.

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.160
Well?

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:35.160
Warm...

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:39.790
This warm feeling...

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.590
How can I describe it...

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:45.550
Ah... I can't put it into words...

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:50.970
Hey, that's your phone.

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.220
Y-Yeah.

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:54.430
Ah... Mitsuki?

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.230
Ah... a job suddenly came up.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.270
Can you come out now?

00:18:57.270 --> 00:18:58.400
Y-Yes.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.060
I'll be outside, then.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.150
I understand.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:03.190
A job suddenly came up.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:04.150
What?

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:04.940
Hurry up.

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:06.490
I'll stay at home.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.110
Okay.

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:31.430
Eh?

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.180
What?!

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:33.430
C-Crap, she's found us!

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:44.940
Did she find out...?

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:46.110
I wonder...

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:47.650
Hazuki...

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:48.450
Eh?

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:56.750
Hazuki...

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:26.320
Music...

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:30.490
I hate music...

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:36.620
Always... taking away everything important to me...

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:06.360
What's that?

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.400
It was a present from my father to my mother.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:11.780
Ooshige-san.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.120
I've found out what I want to say.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.450
What is it?

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.290
I want to make people feel warm inside with my music.

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:23.040
I even want people who hate music...

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.750
...fall in love with music.

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:07.230
Takuto! We've got a problem!

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:08.690
<i>Full Moon</i>  and Dr. Wakaouji...

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:11.860
A magazine says that they're having a steamy love affair! {edited}

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:12.730
Huh?

00:23:12.730 --> 00:23:14.690
That can't possibly be true!

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:16.570
How did that happen?

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:19.570
It's gotta be the work of Wakamatsu Madoka again!

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:22.280
Even up to the bitter end... that girl...

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:24.500
One problem down, and another pops up, huh?

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:27.000
At this rate, we'll never get to the recording!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:28.830
What are we supposed to do?!

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:31.000
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.000
I Will not Lose
